course: dictionary
lesson: 1966
title: Competitive
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Competitive means wanting very much to win, or to do better than others. It can also describe a game, a sport or prices where people try to beat each other.
explain: Look at the words around it. «There is no return to competitive sport for at least 21 days after a concussion» tells you that competitive sport is sport where players try to win against each other. Swap your meaning into the sentence: "no return to sport where players try to win" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Competitive changes its form: competitive, more competitive, most competitive. Notice what it describes, such as sport, games or prices, so you know which meaning fits.
fact: Competitive means wanting to win, or involving competition.
fact: «Competitive sport» means sport where players or teams try to beat each other.
fact: «Competitive prices» means prices that are as good as or cheaper than others.
fact: A concussion is a knock to the head, and «after a concussion» means straight after one has happened.
fact: Competitive is an adjective: competitive, more competitive, most competitive.
exercise: «After a concussion, UK grassroots guidance allows no competitive sport for at least 21 days.» What does competitive sport mean? | Sport only for adults | *Sport where players try to beat each other | Sport that is free to watch | Sport done quietly on your own
exercise: A shop has competitive prices. What does that suggest? | Its prices are very high | It only sells food | *Its prices are as good as or cheaper than others | Its prices change every hour
exercise: Nadia is very competitive in every board game. What does competitive mean here? | Never plays games | Plays only quiet games | *Wants very much to win | Is afraid of games
test:  The team had a competitive spirit, so they never gave up. What does competitive spirit suggest? | Not caring about the score | Liking to sit on the bench | Being sleepy after a long game | *Wanting very much to win
test: Which word is the most (highest) form of competitive? | compete | more competitive | competition | *most competitive
exam: Which phrase means prices as good as or cheaper than others? | Silly prices | *Competitive prices | Very expensive prices | Hidden prices
